  "qualityCriteria": {
    "status": "root-frozen-before-editor",
    "definitionOfGood": "A rounded low blue/cyan stone shelf with purposeful readable slab construction, broad soft non-directional lighting, and clean same-profile repeatable joins in every required facing and actual intended size.",
    "priorityOutcomes": [
      {
        "id": "volume",
        "priority": 1,
        "outcome": "A broad low blue rock shelf with useful rounded slab volume, clear shoulder/front/top relationships and a coherent stone construction in all4 facings. Rebuild the interior/crown/secondary forms freely within locked envelope; original blank loft, three straight crack sticks and four-part topology are not constraints. Preserve the exact true W/E finite section, not a tall-wall form."
      },
      {
        "id": "materials-color",
        "priority": 2,
        "outcome": "Blue/cyan original palette family with clear soft cyan upper surfaces, readable mid-blue body and restrained darker recesses; secondary pebbles/accents may be distinct but subordinate. Material and shape separation survives logical128cell and phone32cell. Avoid a near-black dead bottom band, muddy merged stone faces or uniform flat cyan expanse."
      },
      {
        "id": "light",
        "priority": 3,
        "outcome": "Broad soft non-directional highlights and gentle modeled plane transitions reveal volume in all four orientations. No preferred horizontal lighting direction, directional ground shadow, sharp white stripe, blown glossy patch or target-derived emissive halo. The dark lower portion retains readable form. Exact shader/light method is editor-owned within registered capture and family continuity."
      },
      {
        "id": "purposeful-detail",
        "priority": 4,
        "outcome": "A few clear major slab breaks, rounded stones, chips or dimples make the ledge feel intentionally built; details support scale and form. Avoid evenly spaced rod-like marks, noisy tiny pits and added detail invisible at use size. Embed/flatten taller target-inspired elements to keep the native0.45 height envelope."
      },
      {
        "id": "artifact-free-all4",
        "priority": 1,
        "outcome": "At source384x704, logical192x352(cell128), and phone32cell, every required facing has complete readable contour and useful surface information. No clipping, black/coplanar patches, dead faces, floating/overlapping props, distracting hard-normal breaks, bright alpha fringe, detached parts, cast shadow, or missing underside/shoulder where visible."
      },
      {
        "id": "repeatability",
        "priority": 1,
        "outcome": "Three same-facing modules join at exactly1worldunit/128logicalpixel pitch using authored handedness. All4 native joined strips and independent captured assemblies show zero visible cracks, bright/dark seams, holes, isolated endcaps or crown steps at internal ports on light/gray/dark, including integer and .25/.5/.75 consumer phases. Equal native finite endpoint profile and matching adjacent material/albedo/normal behavior are necessary; counts/hashes alone cannot pass appearance."
      }
    ],
    "hardConstraints": [
      "Registered55.0079798014degree orthographic square-grid capture governs; saved35degree presentation camera is incidental. Logical192x352/root96,248/cell128; native4x768x1408/root384,992; published2x384x704/root192,496. Preserve actual matrices/aspect1.22065556 and all4 cardinal root rotations. Explicit source-study reconciliation: common native filter_size0.5 persisted and whole native4x-to-published2x BOX reduction replace historical filter1.5/LANCZOS. Native lighting/materials may improve symmetrically for the style and continuity; one recipe for all views and strips. Actual common canvas nearest AFTER resize, ordinary final wholecanvas filtering, no fitting/cropping/shifting/overlap/alpha or RGB repair/perview recolor.",
      "True W/E ports are localX=-.5/+ .5 at pitch1. Their exact finite ordered(Y,Z) section is [(-.45,0),(.45,0),(.45,.28),(.39,.43),(-.39,.43),(-.45,.28)]. Preserve actual finite base x[-.5,.5],y[-.45,.45],z0; intentional nonport ground margins are not gaps. Native allowed envelope[-.5,-.45,0]..[.5,.45,.45], tolerance1e-5world for float representation, never design extension. No tall-wall/full1x1 opaque-ground law, endpoint bevel gap, cap rounding, overhang or arbitrary overlap.",
      "At both true cutplanes, exposed adjacent native profile/albedo/material behavior and rendered normals must match under authored same-handed W/E connection. First middle may design a better canonical material/normal field, but both endpoints and their neighboring bands must actually evaluate continuously; labels/AABB alone do not prove this. Measure evaluated finite sections, ordered normals, albedo/resource signatures and intermediate boundary samples. No exposed internal endcaps/steps/dark rods/bright fringes. Retain broad finite-area-light native-versus-independent RGB residuals honestly, separate from actual local boundary defects; approval requires visibly clean all4 native and independent joins at use sizes. Later edge/corner/end receive fresh independent pairs and reuse the exact approved canonical resources; no family approval inferred.",
      "Static1frame/nativeframe1/12fps/nonloop; no added animation or gameplay."
    ],
    "requiredEvidence": [
      "Exact sealed editable .blend with explicit private object/material/light ownership and all nonpacked dependencies in minimal resource closure.",
      "Every static N/E/S/W native source4x and published2x full canvas, plus four-view native/logical/phone sheet with light/gray/dark composites.",
      "All4 native3middle strips and independent3middle assemblies with true root/pitch; transparent native outputs, cutface local RGB+alpha masks and actual common-nativecanvas consumer screenshots logical128/phone32 at integer and representative fractional phases.",
      "Native evaluated endpoint sections/normals/albedo/resource signatures and actual static action/material-animation checks. No image fitting, warps, pixel alpha/RGB repairs, overlap, per-facing recolor or phase nudges.",
      "Later exact packet review follows frozen REVIEW-COVERAGE; no initial/preparation/family acceptance is inferred."
    ],
